    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "datasource",
        "uid": "grafana"
      },
      "description": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 21
      },
      "id": 9,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "**Routing Infrastructure Units (RIU)** determine hub router capacity:\n\n| RIU | Throughput | Supported Spoke VMs |\n|-----|------------|---------------------|\n| 1 | 1 Gbps | 500 |\n| 2 | 2 Gbps | 2,000 |\n| 3 | 3 Gbps | 5,000 |\n| 4-5 | 4-5 Gbps | 10,000-10,001+ |\n\n- **Spoke VM Utilization** near 100% means you must increase RIU before adding spokes.\n- **Data Processed** only covers flows traversing the hub router; with routing intent, most traffic is handled by the firewall instead.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "title": "About Routing Infrastructure Units",
      "type": "text"
    },
